# Future ideas / backlog

Implemented in the current version:

- [x] HMAC challenge-response room authentication.
- [x] Configurable per-file and total room-storage limits.
- [x] SHA-256 checksums for transferred files.
- [x] Atomic client downloads using temporary `.part` files.
- [x] Upload progress display.
- [x] Heartbeat messages and idle connection timeouts.
- [x] Timestamps on room messages.
- [x] `/who` participant listing.
- [x] `/msg <nickname> <text>` private messages.
- [x] `/history` recent room history.
- [x] Learner documentation in `GUIDE.md`.
- [x] Tests for the authentication exchange and configuration.

## Remaining security work

- [ ] Add certificate-based server identity verification and optional certificate pinning.
- [ ] Add a carefully reviewed ephemeral key exchange for forward secrecy.
- [ ] Replace the shared global-room password design with explicit room invitations or access tokens.
- [ ] Add an option to require private rooms only and disable open-room mode.
- [ ] Add secure password guidance and avoid showing sensitive values in logs or errors.
- [ ] Add rate limits for authentication attempts, messages, and file requests.

## Remaining reliability and transfer work

- [ ] Add automated reconnect with a clear session state.
- [ ] Add resumable uploads and downloads with chunk offsets.
- [ ] Add transfer cancellation.
- [ ] Add safer ZIP extraction with path traversal checks if automatic unpacking is added.
- [ ] Add a server-side quota reservation so simultaneous uploads cannot exceed room storage.

## Remaining chat and user-experience work

- [x] Add clearer first-run setup instead of asking many raw questions.
- [x] Add command autocomplete where the terminal provides `readline` and command-specific help.
- [x] Add colored message types and optional desktop/terminal notifications.
- [x] Add configurable and remembered download folders.
- [x] Add room-owner controls such as muting, kicking, or banning participants.
- [x] Add typing indicators or a composing status.

## Remaining architecture and distribution work

- [ ] Add protocol-version negotiation and capability discovery.
- [x] Add integration tests using local host/client sockets.
- [x] Fix the reported bugs in `errors.txt` (upload paths, `/quit` shutdown crash, command edges) and harden the control protocol.
- [ ] Add structured logging with configurable verbosity.
- [ ] Split `chat.py` into protocol, crypto, file-transfer, room-state, and UI modules.
- [ ] Add a graphical interface while keeping the terminal interface.
- [ ] Package the program as a standalone executable for Windows, macOS, and Linux.
